				5214,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Expand trusted paths and add executable magic-number detection\n\nSubmodule sync bringing three complementary improvements for extension runtime reliability:\n1. **Extended trusted paths** (`PathSecurity.rs`): Add `/tmp`, `/private/tmp`, `/var/tmp` for language servers (ruby-lsp, pyright, etc.), third-party tool state (`~/.gitkraken`, `~/.copilot`, `~/.config/git`), and read-only POSIX OS files.\n2. **Magic-number executable detection** (`VsixInstaller.rs`): Probe file headers for ELF, Mach-O fat/thin, and shebang. Detect bin paths (`bin/`, `server/`, `tools/`, `omnisharp`, `adapter`, `native`) and promote 0o644 → 0o755 for detected executables, fixing EACCES on spawn. Add `HealExecutableBits()` for retroactive fixes.\n3. **Boot-time exec-bit heal** (`Scanner.rs`): Walk user extensions (`~/.land/extensions/`) at scan time to recover extensions installed before the fix.\n\nImpact: Extension binaries (rust-analyzer, GitLens, Copilot) that were failing with EACCES due to missing exec bits now run correctly.",
			"SHA": "6df08625901c15474baf39bc8680dd4bc9ae9dd6"
		}
